WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:04.234
I'm here are Tariq Trotter
from the Roots.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:07.300
And we are about to face off
in the first-ever

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.067
"Tonight show" Ford Electric
Cooler Scooter Race.

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:11.868
Here we go!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.601
Now, we will each be riding

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.467
these custom-made
scooter sleighs,

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:19.501
which match the two
new Ford Mustang Mach-E SUVs

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:23.300
parked downstairs
here at 30 Rockefeller Plaza.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.133
I am riding red.
Tariq is riding blue.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.200
They've been charging both of
these scooters all day long.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.868
And I've been told
they can go upwards

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:31.868
of 3 to 5 miles per hour.

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.167
-Whoo!

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:34.834
-So let's be careful out there,
Tariq.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.801
Alright.
Here's how the race works.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:38.667
We're going to head out
these doors, okay?

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.434
Past Hashtag the Panda,

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.934
who is untangling a ball
of Christmas lights.

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:45.601
Then we're gonna go towards the
elevators, loop around Santa,

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:49.734
who is charging his sleigh with
a Ford electric charging
station.

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:52.067
We'll turn back down the hallway

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.501
past an ugly Christmas sweater
party.

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.834
Then we'll be careful
to avoid the gingerbread houses

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.901
in the dangerous
Gingerbread Man's Curve.

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:01.033
And for the last leg
of the race,

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:03.501
we have to drive through
the Christmas tree car wash...

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:06.934
then dodge snowballs
thrown by an angry yeti.

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.901
The first one
to make it back to the studio

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:12.167
and smash through
the pyramid of presents

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.801
will win and be the champion.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, my God.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:17.601
-That good?
-Yeah.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:20.367
-Higgins, count us down.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.801
-Are you guys ready?
-Yes.

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:24.767
-One, two, three, go!

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:26.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.501
[ Indistinct conversation ]

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.400
♪♪

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.167
-Alright. Where are you?
I can feel you.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.601
Whah!

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:36.634
♪♪

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:38.334
-Aah! [ Laughs ]

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.767
-Be careful.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.467
-Crashed.

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.534
-What are you doing?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.167
-Someone call the police.

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:49.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.467
-You ran me off the road, man.

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:55.667
-Oh, my God. This is hilarious.
Hey. Someone call 911.

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.501
-My gosh.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:59.200
-Now you got it in reverse.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.601
-My gosh. I got this.

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.167
-Whoo!

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:13.267
♪♪

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:15.801
-Aah!

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:20.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.801
-Oh, my God.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:29.567
♪♪

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:33.267
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:40.801
♪♪

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:48.300
♪♪

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.934
-Whoo!

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:56.200
♪♪

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.534
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:57.534 --> 00:03:00.734
♪♪

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:05.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.434
-We did it!

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:17.934
Whoo!
-Just like rehearsal.

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:20.067
-Yep. Perfect.

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:24.067
-Oh, my gosh. Congratulations.

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:26.234
Get off that thing.
Get off that thing.

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:28.367
Congratulations.
Tariq Trotter is the winner.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:29.601
-Whoo!

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:32.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you!

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.200
-Ohh. Oh, my God.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.601
That was really fun.
But we're not finished.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:41.267
We want to pick someone special
from the audience

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.100
to help us with this next part.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.901
Simone Beadie?

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:47.667
Simone Beadie? Are you there?

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:57.534
♪♪

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.868
Hi. Nice to meet you.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:01.234
-Nice to meet you.
-Jimmy. That's Tariq.

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:02.467
-Nice to meet you, too.

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:04.133
-Simone, is it Baity or Beadie?
-It's Beadie.

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:05.567
-Simone Beadie.
I got it right. Good.

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:06.968
Simone, where are you from?

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:09.400
-I am from Northern Virginia,
like the D.C. area.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.801
-Oh, very cool.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.801
And what do you do for a living?

00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:16.067
-I am a middle-school
math teacher.

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:17.367
-Hey!

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:20.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:23.300
We love math teachers. Thank you
so much for being here.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.033
We actually knew
that you were coming tonight.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.367
We talked to people
before the show started.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.834
It's the holiday season,

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.133
which is all about giving
and helping those in need.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:33.734
So our friends at Ford
and the Ford Motor Company Fund

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:37.133
will be donating $100,000
to Feeding America.

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:40.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:43.334
And can we look
at those cars again?

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:45.868
They're also -- They filled
the Mustang Mach-E

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.868
front trunks, or "frunks,"

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:51.067
with food that will be donated
in your name

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:52.934
to a local
Feeding America food bank.

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:55.000
-Ohh! Thank you so much.
That's awesome.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.234
-Feels good for the holidays.
Go to feedingamerica.org

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.667
to find out how you can make

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.234
a difference
in your own community.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.334
Thank you so much, Simone.
Thank you for being here.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:04.767
-Thank you so much.
-I appreciate it.

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:07.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:10.734
We'll be right --
Actually, wait. Hold a second.

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:13.567
Simone, while you're here,
one more thing.

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:16.267
Ford wants to do something else
special for you.

00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:18.400
That's why they're giving you

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.367
a brand-new, all-electric
Ford Mustang Mach-E!

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:25.133
-Oh, my God!

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:29.000
-Goodbye, gas. Hello, freedom.
The high-performance,

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.434
all-electric
Ford Mustang Mach-E SUV

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:33.300
gives you zero-to-60
exhilaration,

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.868
expansive range,
and zero tailpipe emissions,

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.234
with the kind of horsepower,
torque, and acceleration

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:39.667
to make you feel like a champion

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:41.567
the moment you slide
into the driver's seat.

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:44.334
The Ford Mach-E.
This ain't no one-trick pony.

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:46.534
Jimmy!
-My thanks to everyone at Ford.

00:05:46.534 --> 00:05:48.501
Stick around.
We'll be right back

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.634
with Regina Hall, everybody!

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:52.367 --> 00:06:01.634
♪♪

